{"game_id":2026020283,"away":"NYR","home":"EDM","split":{"name":"Jones","side":1,"sec":1850},"lede":"Edmonton had last change, so Mike Babcock picked most of these matchups. Edmonton played without Colton Dach and Filip Hållander and lost Max Jones after 10:50 of the second. The Rangers played without Alberts Šmits and Matt Rempe.","notes":[{"kind":"match","head":"Nugent-Hopkins’s line drew Dorofeyev’s line","text":"Mike Babcock sent Kapanen, Nugent-Hopkins and Hyman out for 7:12 of their 11:36 at 5-on-5 against Kartye, Miller and Dorofeyev (62%, about 32% with no line matching), and the chances were close, 0.27 to 0.34 expected goals."},{"kind":"match","head":"McDavid’s line drew Zibanejad’s line","text":"Podkolzin, McDavid and Draisaitl spent 7:38 of their 14:22 at 5-on-5 against Perreault, Zibanejad and Lafrenière (53%, about 32% with no line matching), and they had the better of the chances, 0.25 to 0.11 expected goals."},{"kind":"swing","head":"One matchup went wrong","text":"Formenton, Dickinson and Joseph kept drawing the Rangers’ third line, Cuylle, Laba and Bjorkstrand. In those 4:23 the Rangers had 0.41 expected goals to Edmonton’s 0.02."},{"kind":"exit","head":"After Jones left, the lines changed but the matchups held","text":"Hyman went from 21% to 39% and Nugent-Hopkins from 21% to 35% of Edmonton’s 5-on-5 time, and Frederic dropped from 21% to 1%. The matchups stayed: Nugent-Hopkins’s line against the Rangers’ second line (64% before, 60% after) and the third line against the Rangers’ third line (50% before, 49% after)."},{"kind":"result","head":"And it went worse","text":"Edmonton had 0.71 to 0.78 expected goals at 5-on-5 before Jones left and 0.36 to 0.71 after. Edmonton led for most of that stretch, though, and a team ahead usually sits back, so the score explains part of it."}],"foot":"Mike Babcock matched about as hard as in his other home games: each line spent 52% of its time against one opposing line, against 36% to 67% in his last ten.","perio